				<h2>ORDINANCE NO. 2026-___</h2>
				<h3>
					AN ORDINANCE ENACTING THE CHILD WELFARE CODE OF THE MUNICIPALITY OF LIBACAO, AKLAN: PROVIDING FOR CHILDREN’S SURVIVAL, DEVELOPMENT, PROTECTION, AND PARTICIPATION, AND ESTABLISHING A LOCAL SUPPORT SYSTEM
				</h3>
				<h3>
					BE IT ORDAINED, as it is hereby ORDAINED by the Sangguniang Bayan of the Municipality of Libacao, Aklan, in session assembled, that:
				</h3>
				<p style="text-align: center">(proposal for an ordinance)</p>
			</article>
			
			<!-- Article 1 Content -->
			<article id="art1" class="article-card">
				<h1 class="articleNumber"><b>ARTICLE 1</b></h1>
				<h1 class="articleTitle">TITLE, POLICIES AND PRINCIPLES, LGU OBLIGATIONS, DEFINITION OF TERMS AND ACRONYMS</h1>
				
				<section id="art1-sec1" class="section-card">
					<h2>SECTION 1. TITLE. —<span class="section-top">This Ordinance shall be known as </span></h2>
					<p style="font-size: 2rem; text-align:center;"><strong>“The Libacao Child Welfare Code”</strong></p>
				</section>

				<section id="art1-sec2" class="section-card">
					<h2>SECTION 2. Declaration Of Policies and Principles. — <span class="section-top">The Municipality of Libacao affirms that every child is important and precious to the community. To this end, the Municipality shall pursue child-centered governance and general welfare by effectively institutionalizing the survival, development, protection, and participation rights of all children. Being a child-loving municipality, it shall ensure that local development is integrated, sustainable, and equitable.</span></h2>
					<p class="section-inner"><b></b></p>
					<p>The Municipal Government of Libacao commits to the holistic protection and development of children through a comprehensive support system. This system shall leverage the active partnership of government agencies, Civil Society Organizations (CSOs), Peoples’ Organizations (POs), and the private sector, all of whom shall serve with the highest degree of professionalism, transparency, and solidarity.</p>
					<p>In all actions concerning children, whether undertaken by public or private social welfare institutions, courts of law, administrative authorities, or legislative bodies, the best interests of the child shall be the primary consideration.</p>
				</section>

				<section id="art1-sec3" class="section-card">
					<h2>SECTION 3. Purposes. — <span class="section-top">This Ordinance is enacted to achieve the following objectives:</span></h2>
					<p><span style="font-weight:bold">To Guarantee Protection:</span> To shield every child against all forms of neglect, abuse, cruelty, exploitation, and other conditions prejudicial to their development;</p>
					<p><span style="font-weight:bold">To Institutionalize Rights:</span> To ensure that children’s rights are prioritized in the programs, budgeting, and decision-making processes of both the municipal government and civil society;</p>
					<p><span style="font-weight:bold">To Promote Holistic Development:</span> To provide a localized framework that advocates for children’s rights and promotes their physical, mental, and social well-being;</p>
					<p><span style="font-weight:bold">To Empower Libacaonon Children:</span> To improve the quality of life for all Libacaonon children, enabling them to fully realize their potential as active participants in community life and nation-building; and</p>
					<p><span style="font-weight:bold">To Establish a Support System:</span> To create a functional and sustainable municipal system that coordinates the efforts of all stakeholders in the delivery of children's services.</p>
				</section>

				<section id="art1-sec4" class="section-card">
					<h2>SECTION 4. Rules of Interpretation. — <span class="section-top">All doubts in the implementation and interpretation of the provisions of this Code, including its Implementing Rules and Regulations, and in all proceedings before any authority shall be resolved liberally in favor of the best interests of the child.</span></h2>
					<p class="section-inner"><b></b></p>
				</section>

				<section id="art1-sec5" class="section-card">
					<h2>SECTION 5. Participation of the Child. — <span class="section-top">All proceedings before any authority shall be conducted in a manner which ensures the right of children to participate and express themselves freely, in accordance with their age and evolving capacities. The Municipality of Libacao shall ensure the meaningful participation of children in the formulation and implementation of policies and programs related to their concerns through the Municipal Council for the Protection of Children (MCPC) or its functional equivalent, and other relevant local bodies.</span></h2>
					<p class="section-inner"><b></b></p>
				</section>

				<section id="art1-sec6" class="section-card">
					<h2>SECTION 6. Duties And Responsibilities of the Municipal Government. — <span class="section-top">Pursuant to Article XV, Section 3, Paragraph 2 of the 1987 Philippine Constitution, the Municipality of Libacao shall defend the rights of children to assistance, including proper healthcare, nutrition, and education, and provide special protection from all forms of neglect, abuse, cruelty, exploitation, and other conditions prejudicial to their development.</span></h2>
					<p>Consistent with the United Nations Convention on the Rights of the Child (UNCRC), the Municipal Government shall, within its jurisdiction:</p>
					<p>a) <span style="font-weight:bold">Implement Legislative and Administrative Measures.</span> Undertake appropriate legislative, administrative, and other measures to implement the rights recognized in the UNCRC. Regarding economic, social, and cultural rights, the Municipal Government shall undertake such measures to the maximum extent of its available resources and, where appropriate, within the framework of inter-agency and international cooperation;</p>
					<p>b) <span style="font-weight:bold">Ensure Survival and Development.</span> Guarantee, to the maximum extent possible, the survival, development, protection, and participation rights of every child;</p>
					<p>c) <span style="font-weight:bold">Provide Comprehensive Protection.</span> Adopt social, educational, and protective measures to shield children from all forms of physical or mental violence, injury or abuse, neglect or negligent treatment, or exploitation including sexual abuse, whether in the custody of parents, legal guardians, or any other person;</p>
					<p>d) <span style="font-weight:bold">Uphold the Right to be Heard.</span> Respect the right of the child to express his/her views freely in all matters affecting them, giving such views due weight in accordance with the age and maturity of the child; and</p>
					<p>e) <span style="font-weight:bold">Support Primary Caregivers.</span> Render appropriate assistance to parents and legal guardians in the performance of their child-rearing responsibilities by ensuring the development of institutions, facilities, and services dedicated to the care of children.</p>
				</section>
			</article>

